1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,766
A quantum computer is not a faster computer.

2
00:00:02,786 --> 00:00:04,541
It is a different kind of machine.

3
00:00:04,561 --> 00:00:07,229
It follows the strangest rules in physics.

4
00:00:07,249 --> 00:00:11,286
And it can solve problems our best
supercomputers could never finish.

5
00:00:12,515 --> 00:00:14,870
Every computer you have used thinks in bits.

6
00:00:14,890 --> 00:00:16,232
Each bit is a switch.

7
00:00:16,252 --> 00:00:17,345
On, or off.

8
00:00:17,365 --> 00:00:18,532
One, or zero.

9
00:00:18,552 --> 00:00:20,732
Your phone holds tens of billions of them.

10
00:00:20,752 --> 00:00:24,882
And that was enough to put a rocket on the
moon, and the internet in your pocket.

11
00:00:24,902 --> 00:00:26,332
But we are hitting a wall.

12
00:00:26,352 --> 00:00:30,677
The switches are the size of atoms now, and
the classical rules stop working.

13
00:00:34,100 --> 00:00:37,300
So instead of fighting it, a quantum
computer uses it.

14
00:00:38,521 --> 00:00:40,601
The quantum bit is called a qubit.

15
00:00:40,621 --> 00:00:42,551
It can be made from one electron.

16
00:00:42,571 --> 00:00:44,951
An electron has a property called spin.

17
00:00:44,971 --> 00:00:48,238
Measure it, and you will find it pointing
up, or down.

18
00:00:48,258 --> 00:00:49,701
Call that one and zero.

19
00:00:49,721 --> 00:00:51,838
But here is where intuition breaks.

20
00:00:51,858 --> 00:00:56,888
Before you measure it, the electron is not
secretly up, and not secretly down.

21
00:00:56,908 --> 00:00:58,276
It is both at once.

22
00:00:58,296 --> 00:01:00,433
Physicists call this superposition.

23
00:01:01,557 --> 00:01:03,841
The classic picture is a spinning coin.

24
00:01:03,861 --> 00:01:07,178
While it spins, it is not heads, and not
tails.

25
00:01:07,198 --> 00:01:09,132
It is a blur of possibility.

26
00:01:09,152 --> 00:01:11,045
Only when it lands does it commit.

27
00:01:11,435 --> 00:01:13,027
Here is where it gets powerful.

28
00:01:13,047 --> 00:01:15,902
Two classical bits hold one of four
patterns.

29
00:01:15,922 --> 00:01:18,265
Two qubits hold all four at once.

30
00:01:18,285 --> 00:01:19,815
Three qubits hold eight.

31
00:01:19,835 --> 00:01:22,477
Add qubits, and the states do not grow.

32
00:01:22,497 --> 00:01:23,565
They explode.

33
00:01:23,585 --> 00:01:28,802
Three hundred qubits hold more states than
there are atoms in the observable universe.

34
00:01:28,822 --> 00:01:30,640
That is not a faster laptop.

35
00:01:30,660 --> 00:01:32,622
That is a new kind of parallelism.

36
00:01:34,403 --> 00:01:36,833
But superposition alone is not enough.

37
00:01:36,853 --> 00:01:39,345
If you measure everything, you get noise.

38
00:01:39,365 --> 00:01:41,758
The second resource is entanglement.

39
00:01:41,778 --> 00:01:46,670
Two entangled qubits share one state, no
matter how far apart they sit.

40
00:01:46,690 --> 00:01:49,783
Measure one, and the other is decided
instantly.

41
00:01:49,803 --> 00:01:52,658
Einstein called it spooky action at a
distance.

42
00:01:52,678 --> 00:01:57,290
It lets a machine spread one problem across
all of its qubits at once.

43
00:01:58,965 --> 00:02:00,573
Then comes the choreography.

44
00:02:00,593 --> 00:02:03,037
Quantum operations do not flip bits.

45
00:02:03,057 --> 00:02:06,811
They rotate probabilities, nudging the
amplitude of each answer.

46
00:02:06,831 --> 00:02:10,548
A good algorithm makes the wrong answers
cancel each other out,

47
00:02:10,568 --> 00:02:13,098
like waves silencing each other in a pond.

48
00:02:13,118 --> 00:02:17,841
The right answer reinforces itself, growing
louder against the silence.

49
00:02:17,861 --> 00:02:19,544
You do not search the haystack.

50
00:02:19,564 --> 00:02:23,302
You tune the universe until the needle is
the only thing left.

51
00:02:24,079 --> 00:02:25,121
And the hard part.

52
00:02:25,141 --> 00:02:28,259
The moment you look, the superposition
collapses.

53
00:02:28,279 --> 00:02:32,534
The machine must stay perfectly isolated,
colder than deep space.

54
00:02:32,554 --> 00:02:35,896
The smallest leak of heat destroys the
calculation.

55
00:02:35,916 --> 00:02:40,504
Today's machines are fragile, and correcting
errors costs most of their power.

56
00:02:41,126 --> 00:02:44,268
This is why quantum computers will not
replace your laptop.

57
00:02:44,288 --> 00:02:46,903
They will model molecules for new drugs,

58
00:02:46,923 --> 00:02:49,868
break encryption, and optimize vast systems.

59
00:02:49,888 --> 00:02:53,443
Because the classical world is a shadow of
the quantum world.

60
00:02:53,463 --> 00:02:57,856
For the first time, we are building machines
that do not calculate about nature.

61
00:02:57,876 --> 00:02:59,638
They work the way nature does.

62
00:03:02,726 --> 00:03:03,881
That is the shift.

63
00:03:03,901 --> 00:03:05,468
Not faster computers.

64
00:03:05,488 --> 00:03:07,726
A new language, for the first time.
